---
import LabsLayout from "../../layouts/labs.astro";
---

<LabsLayout title="Scenario F — External Parquet ingest — Querial Labs" active="f">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-querial-indigo-on-dark">Scenario F</p>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mt-1">External Parquet ingest</h1>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-3">
                Upload a tiny Parquet file at <strong class="text-foreground">trigger</strong>
                time. Querial seeds it as the <code class="text-foreground">ids</code>
                artifact, then Staged Database SQL upserts PostgreSQL
                <code class="text-foreground">ingest.ids</code>. This scenario does
                <strong class="text-foreground">not</strong> read AdventureWorks and
                <strong class="text-foreground">must not be scheduled</strong>.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <a href="/labs/adventureworks/downloads/scenario-f-ingest.zip" download
               class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg bg-querial-indigo px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-white hover:opacity-90">
                Download scenario-f-ingest.zip
            </a>
            <a href="/labs/adventureworks/source/fixtures/tiny-ids.parquet" download
               class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-border/60 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-muted/50">
                Download tiny-ids.parquet
            </a>
            <a href="/labs/run-through" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-border/60 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-muted/50">
                Load and test
            </a>
            <a href="/docs/developer-external-parquet" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-border/60 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-muted/50">
                External Parquet docs
            </a>
            <a href="/docs/developer-handler-contracts" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-border/60 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-muted/50">
                Handler contracts
            </a>
        </div>

        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 [&>p]:text-muted-foreground [&>h2]:text-foreground">
            <h2>Package</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li>Package <code class="text-foreground">aw-scenario-f</code>, pipeline <code class="text-foreground">aw_scenario_f</code>.</li>
                <li>Stub: <code class="text-foreground">aw-pg-dest</code> only (same warehouse as B–E).</li>
                <li>Typed parameter <code class="text-foreground">batch_label</code> (string, required, default <code class="text-foreground">lab</code>). The sink table does not store it; it exists so Run now shows a field next to the file.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Topology</h2>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>ingest_ids  (ROOT, external-parquet, outputName: ids)
  └─(artifact_available)→ load_ids  (staged-database-sql → aw-pg-dest)</code></pre>
            <p>
                The ingest node has no SQL and no connection. The control plane seeds
                the file before readiness. Downstream
                <code class="text-foreground">from_step</code> still means
                <em>same run</em>.
            </p>

            <h2>Migrations (aw-pg-dest)</h2>
            <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li><code class="text-foreground">ingest_001_create_schema</code> — <code class="text-foreground">CREATE SCHEMA ingest</code></li>
                <li><code class="text-foreground">ingest_002_create_ids</code> — <code class="text-foreground">ingest.ids</code> (<code class="text-foreground">id</code> PK)</li>
            </ol>
            <p>Use deployment <code class="text-foreground">before_run</code> on first pass.</p>

            <h2>Steps and config</h2>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>config:
  outputName: ids
  retentionDays: 30

config:
  stages:
    - from_step: ingest_ids
      columns:
        - source: id
          name: id
          type: int
          nullable: false
  transaction:
    mode: stage-and-execute</code></pre>
            <p>
                Package YAML is a <strong class="text-foreground">list</strong>, not a
                map keyed by alias. Sink SQL uses the bare token because this step has
                one inbound file:
            </p>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>INSERT INTO ingest.ids (id, loaded_at_utc)
SELECT s.id, (now() AT TIME ZONE 'utc')
FROM {"{{ stage }}"} AS s
ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET loaded_at_utc = EXCLUDED.loaded_at_utc;</code></pre>
            <p>
                Designer: draw the artifact edge; Fill columns from a sample upload or
                the last ingest artifact — never FMTONLY on the sink.
                <a href="/docs/developer-handler-contracts" class="text-link hover:underline">Step handler contracts</a>.
            </p>

            <h2>Fixture</h2>
            <p>
                Multipart field name: <code class="text-foreground">parquet.ids</code>
                (prefix plus the producer <code class="text-foreground">outputName</code>).
                Canonical file: <code class="text-foreground">fixtures/tiny-ids.parquet</code>
                (three-row <code class="text-foreground">id</code> column). The zip also
                ships it under the package tree.
            </p>

            <h2>Flags</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li><code class="text-foreground">Querial:Extensions:Artifacts=true</code></li>
                <li><code class="text-foreground">Querial:Extensions:DagExecution=true</code></li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                DuckDB is not required for F (no extract/transform). Legacy serial
                execution must not run <code class="text-foreground">external-parquet</code>.
            </p>

            <h2>Walkthrough extras</h2>
            <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2">
                <li>Import the zip. Resolve <code class="text-foreground">aw-pg-dest</code> only.</li>
                <li>Designer: ingest node has no connection badge and no SQL editor. One inbound artifact edge on the sink. Column overlay is the contract UI.</li>
                <li>Publish: one root. Do <strong class="text-foreground">not</strong> create a schedule — create/enable is refused; a leftover fire fails closed.</li>
                <li>Run now: set <code class="text-foreground">batch_label</code>, attach the fixture as <code class="text-foreground">parquet.ids</code>. JSON-only trigger is 400. See <a href="/docs/devops-trigger" class="text-link hover:underline">Trigger API and Run now</a>.</li>
                <li>Run Graph: ingest is already Succeeded (seeded). Load stages and upserts. Artifact details show expiry.</li>
            </ol>

            <h2>Verify</h2>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>SELECT id, loaded_at_utc FROM ingest.ids ORDER BY id;</code></pre>
            <p>Expect three ids from the fixture. Re-run with the same file is an upsert on <code class="text-foreground">id</code>.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</LabsLayout>
